# How it works {% #how-it-works %}

When a pull request is opened or gets new commits, Appwrite queues a review. The reviewer checks out the pull request and reads the repository, not only the diff. At Normal and Expert [strength](/docs/products/reviews/strength), it can also run your tests and type checkers in a sandbox. A second pass checks every finding against the code before the review is posted.

Each review has four parts:

- **Summary**: What the pull request changes.
- **Findings**: Problems on the lines they concern, each with a severity of **Critical**, **Major**, **Minor**, or **Info**.
- **Verdict**: **Approved**, **Changes requested**, or **Commented**.
- **Merge confidence**: A grade from **S**, ready to merge, down to **F**, do not merge.

